entries.note:
Tiles 1:1 with the source resources touched, gathered by a collection:
home.component.ts (registry model: clientSeenAt/isClientDormant, opener identity, 180d dead-row purge that also drops orphaned name overrides, DCP-local rename override);
home.component.html (one row at rest + the others-disclosure + inline rename; every row emits the SAME cells or the columns go ragged);
home.component.scss (the SECTION owns the column tracks, rows borrow via subgrid; fit-content caps the handle because minmax(0,15rem) is grown to full width by the maximize-tracks step);
portal-overlay.component.ts (roster now carries each install lastSeen as s — without it every entry was stamped now on each handoff and nothing could ever go dormant);
i18n catalogs (dcp.clients* x14).

Pheromones: mark each part for what it IS (registry-model / view / style / handoff / catalog) so render and behaviour resolve from the mark.

The WHY the notes must carry: 27 lookalike chips, because the display name is a browser brand (edge/chrome), the only distinguishing field was hidden in a title tooltip, the version rendered as NOTHING when the package would not resolve, and nothing ever pruned. Jaime pushed twice — first why show old rows by default, then why show more rows than the very latest — and the answer both times was that we should not: the resting list is now the install you are managing FROM, everything else behind a count.

NOT safely re-runnable: note-add is additive.
